# Azure migration - credentials, local CLI state, and any generated
# infra-as-code output never belong in the repo (see azure/ once it
# exists - ARM/Bicep *source* templates we hand-author are fine to
# commit, this is about generated/secret output only).
.azure/
azure/**/*.parameters.local.json
azure/**/.terraform/
azure/**/terraform.tfstate
azure/**/terraform.tfstate.backup
azure/**/*.tfvars
!azure/**/*.tfvars.example
# terraform plan output - a saved `terraform plan -out=...` file embeds
# the full resulting resource state (real IPs, resource IDs, etc.),
# same sensitivity class as tfstate above and just as prone to going
# stale - never meant to be committed, caught live 2026-08-30 not being
# covered by the tfstate rule above (it's a custom-named plan file, not
# named terraform.tfstate) right before it would have leaked a real
# public IP address into the repo.
azure/**/tfplan
azure/**/*.tfplan
*.pfx
*.publishsettings
kubeconfig
kubeconfig.*
*.kubeconfig













